University FAQ Chatbot

A simple FAQ chatbot built with Flask and scikit-learn. It matches a user's question to the most similar question in a FAQ list using TF-IDF and cosine similarity, then returns the stored answer. If nothing is similar enough, it politely points the user to the relevant department.

Features
Answers questions by matching them to a list of FAQs in faqs.json
TF-IDF with unigrams and bigrams for better phrase matching
Adjustable similarity threshold to control how strict matching is
Input validation (valid JSON, non-empty question, max 500 characters)
Simple JSON API plus a web page for chatting
Tech Stack
Python 3
Flask
scikit-learn
Project Structure
.
├── app1.py          # Flask app and matching logic
├── faqs.json        # FAQ questions and answers
├── template/
│   └── index.html   # Chat page
└── requirements.txt
Getting Started
Clone the repository
bash
   git clone <your-repo-url>
   cd <your-repo-folder>
Create a virtual environment (optional but recommended)
bash
   python -m venv venv
   source venv/bin/activate    # On Windows: venv\Scripts\activate
Install dependencies
bash
   pip install flask scikit-learn
Run the app
bash
   python app1.py
Open http://127.0.0.1:5000 in your browser.
FAQ Data Format

Add or edit entries in faqs.json. It must be a non-empty list, and every item needs a non-empty question and answer:

json
[
  {
    "question": "How do I apply for admission?",
    "answer": "You can apply online through the university admissions portal."
  },
  {
    "question": "When is the fee submission deadline?",
    "answer": "Please check the academic calendar for the current deadline."
  }
]

Restart the app after changing faqs.json.

API
POST /chat

Request

json
{ "question": "How can I apply for admission?" }

Response

json
{
  "answer": "You can apply online through the university admissions portal.",
  "matched_question": "How do I apply for admission?",
  "similarity": 0.62,
  "matched": true
}

If no FAQ is similar enough, matched is false, matched_question is null, and a fallback message is returned.

Errors return HTTP 400 with an error message (invalid JSON, empty question, or question longer than 500 characters).

Configuration

The matching strictness is controlled by SIMILARITY_THRESHOLD in app1.py (default 0.25).

Raise it for fewer, more accurate matches
Lower it to answer more questions, with a higher chance of wrong matches

Test with real student questions to find a good value.

How It Works
All FAQ questions are converted into TF-IDF vectors at startup.
The user's question is transformed with the same vectorizer.
Cosine similarity is calculated against every FAQ question.
The best match is returned if its score meets the threshold; otherwise a fallback message is shown.
Possible Improvements
Add more FAQs and alternative phrasings for each question
Use sentence embeddings for better semantic matching
Add tests for the matching logic
Deploy with a production server such as Gunicorn
